    #      27, and part 5 P2's own comparison (cmp.py), extracted from
    #      records/logs/m1p5-p2/run.log and checked against the hash that log
    #      printed, run on every host pair, with its planted-flag controls on the
    #      first workbook (P1 ruling 10); the record checked against the run
    #      directory, table by table, and its family rows derived here
    #      (specs/0014 P2 verification ruling 5);
    #   3. the keep regenerated: cargo test for the workspace on the host with
    #      EMEND_KEEP_DIR naming <keep>, and on i686-unknown-linux-musl into a
    #      second keep; the same counts and names as this phase's test.log; the
    #      two keeps compared byte for byte; the host keep compared, name for name
    #      and hash for hash, with part 8 P2's committed open-check record (no .rs
    #      file changed since, test.log);
    #   4. the edit open check on the host keep (specs/0016 "Harness runs", from
    #      part 8's decision 3), recorded as m2p1-open-<utc-date>-<shortsha>.md
    #      and .txt (P1 ruling 7), installed into records/ by a command this log
    #      prints; the record against the keep row by row, its .md derived from
    #      its .txt with the heading specs/0015 P2 verification ruling 1 gives, the
    #      verdicts against part 8 P2's record, and the acceptance: no output
    #      refused on an accepted input, no count that differs, no error;
    #   5. the Excel check 2 list: scripts/excel-check-list.py with --run part 6
    #      P3's run directory, --run-plain this log's style-sample run directory,
    #      the keep and the new record; every hash in it checked against the file
    #      it names; corpus rows 54, fixture and input rows two per accepted pair,
    #      counted; the references against part 6 P2's own derivation, as part 8
    #      P2 did;
    #   6. the staged directory for the maintainer (P1 ruling 4): the list as
    #      excel-check-list.txt, scripts/excel-check-open.ps1 from the phase
    #      commit, and every listed file at files/<source>/<file>, each hash
    #      checked again; zipped outside the repository, its sha256 printed.
    # No corpus reference, value or text is printed: the references are compared
    # and counted only and live in the list, which is not committed; the log
    # prints the list's and the zip's sha256 and byte counts.
    #
    # WRITTEN FOR M2 part 1 P1 from part 8 P2's run script (printed in
